// endpoint_get_agent_by_vendor_task.proto — GetAgentByVendorTask: WHICH AGENT
// a vendor task locator names, within the lineage of the caller's main agent.
//
// WHY THE SHIM ASKS. A subagent's vendor task id is the agent's own LOCATOR
// (the `<id>` of `agent-<id>.jsonl`), and it comes back when the agent is
// RESUMED — but the resume's `task_started` names the call that woke it (a
// `SendMessage`), not the spawn whose `tool_use_id` IS the agent under the
// cross-plane minting rule. A shim that saw the spawn remembers the pairing;
// a shim that restarted since did not, and could not name the running agent at
// all (2026-09-27: the resumed agent never reached the live set or the footer).
//
// WHY THE STORE CAN ANSWER. The sidecar reads both halves of the pairing from
// the vendor's own files — the locator from the transcript's file name, the
// spawning `tool_use_id` from its meta file — and writes them with the agent's
// first rows (`EntryBatch.agent_locators`). An agent can only be resumed after
// it has run, so its pairing is on record long before a resume asks for it,
// and the shim never reads a vendor file itself.
//
